# Commits that touched a lot of lines without changing any code — so that
# `git blame` keeps pointing at whoever actually wrote each line.
#
# GitHub reads this file automatically in its own blame view. To get the same
# locally, once per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Only add a commit here if it is genuinely non-semantic (a reformat, a line-
# ending normalization, a bulk rename). Never a behaviour change.
#
# Two things to know before editing, both verified against this repo:
#
#   * FULL 40-character sha only. An abbreviated one makes blame fail outright
#     ("fatal: invalid object name"), for everyone who has the config above set.
#
#   * A sha that isn't in the repo is silently ignored — no warning, blame just
#     quietly stops skipping that commit. So if an entry below ever gets
#     rewritten (a squash or rebase merge gives it a new sha), this file goes
#     back to doing nothing and nothing tells you. Re-point it.

# Normalize line endings to LF (introduced .gitattributes). Rewrote every line
# of the Rust files under src-tauri/ that had been committed with CRLF, by
# stripping CRs and nothing else, so it would otherwise have taken over blame
# for all of them.
